// PLANNED/OPEN semantic fixture contract. This is intentionally not valid,
// runnable Pergyra source and is not an aggregate-gate input.
//
// The step-local typed binding spelling is fixed as
// `on outcome: subject.Action(...);`. Typed variant branching, success-only
// completion evidence, carried predecessor identity, and compensation syntax
// are not fixed yet. Do not implement this fixture by hiding the outcome in a
// subject field, converting it to Bool/literal expect, or matching variant-name
// strings.
//
// Required scenario:
//
// subject WorkflowActor owns observable forward/compensation counters/state.
// action A returns OutcomeA::Succeeded(ReceiptA) or Failed(FailureA).
// action B consumes ReceiptA and returns OutcomeB::Succeeded(ReceiptB) or
// Failed(FailureB).
// compensation action UndoA consumes exact predecessor-A evidence.
// compensation action UndoB exists so the failure run can prove it was not run.
//
// Success execution:
//   bind A outcome -> success case ReceiptA payload is consumed by B
//   bind B outcome -> success case ReceiptB payload changes final observation
//   UndoA=0, UndoB=0
//
// Failure execution:
//   A succeeds and produces a consumed ReceiptA
//   B returns a typed FailureB whose payload changes the exact failure output
//   B has no success-completion fact
//   rollback follows B -> A predecessor evidence
//   UndoA=1, UndoB=0, final forward state restored
//
// The implemented fixture must have a success run and a real injected failure
// run. Merely parsing these declarations or emitting carrier names is not
// executable evidence.
